<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sabit Damulla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1934">1934</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sabit Damulla Abdulbaki</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sabit Damulla was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> Islamic scholar and nationalist from Atush who became prime minister of the First East Turkestan Republic, proclaimed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgar">Kashgar</a> in November 1933. The republic sought an Islamic state independent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. It fell to the Hui forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ma-zhongying">Ma Zhongying</a> in 1934, and Sabit Damulla was captured and executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sabit-damulla.jpg" alt="Sabit Damulla" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sabit_Damolla_Abdulbaki.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
